  "sourceFitAssessment": {
    "learnerTask": "Compare one cytokine contacting distinct cell types and distributing beyond its origin",
    "gap": "Flow lacks physical receivers and local-versus-systemic spread",
    "accuracyGuardrails": "No fight-cancer instruction; receptor/state dependent; local production can spread; class not one indication",
    "baselinePageSHA256": "9cbdc936230de197c25509cb50341e050d629ff9858b2ad377fc2c38bdd97c23",
    "currentVisualFit": "adequate",
    "humanReview": "pending",
    "reasoning": "Two cells receive the same generic cytokine symbols but differ in surface receivers and labeled internal state. A second scene follows conditional circulation toward another tissue, explicitly requiring arrival and persistence. This supplements, rather than duplicates, the retained spatial-average diagram. The caption and practice separate cell response from molecular identity and local origin from confinement; the footer keeps receptor engagement separate from tumor killing. No exposure recipe, regimen or benefit ranking is inferred."
  },
